# Template for shell/shared/opencode.env (gitignored).
# Copy to opencode.env and fill in locally. Format is KEY=value (no `export`),
# so install.sh, the login shell, and the systemd unit can all read it.
#
# The shared server on :15001 is the managed background service. Its password
# lives in ~/.config/opencode/service.json and is generated per host; there is
# no OPENCODE_PASSWORD to set here.
#
# Keep secrets here, not in service.json: bare `opencode service get` prints
# every value stored in that file. This file is 0600 and gitignored.
# Linux reads it through the unit's EnvironmentFile; macOS inherits it from the
# shell that spawns the service, so restart the service after editing.
# ntfy topic for the plugins/ntfy TUI plugin. Unset skips ntfy; the native
# desktop notification still fires.
OPENCODE_NTFY_TOPIC=
# ntfy base URL. Unset => https://ntfy.sh. Point at the self-hosted server
# (e.g. http://host:15002) to keep notification bodies on your own machine.
OPENCODE_NTFY_SERVER=
# Bearer token for a self-hosted ntfy with auth enabled (`ntfy token add`).
OPENCODE_NTFY_TOKEN=
# OpenCode server URL for the ntfy notification click-through. Set per machine to
# a URL reachable from the device that taps the notification; use THIS machine's
# tailnet MagicDNS URL, never another machine's:
#   http://<this-machine>.<tailnet>.ts.net:15001

# Project credentials for ad-hoc agent commands (psql, stripe). Global so a
# session in any directory can reach prod when asked; move them to a project's
# .env if that reach is wider than needed.
CNTCTUS_POSTGRES_PROD_URL=
CNTCTUS_STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=
CNTCTUS_POSTHOG_API_KEY=
